%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b2c8c673688eb5f49beb593911c9d414, type: 3}
  m_Name: InfoTexts
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: ArtnetFixture.Core::InfoTextsScriptableObject
  generalInfo: 'This device functions as a virtual lighting fixture.



    Video
    output from the device is controlled

    by incoming DMX data over the network.



    Connect
    a lighting controller on the same

    network to control the fixture.'
  fixtureName: The name of this fixture as it appears on the network and in the Web
    UI.
  ipAddress: Advanced Network settings.
  webUi: 'You can access the Web UI from another device on the same network to configure
    fixture settings remotely.


    Scan the QR Code or open this address in a web
    browser :



    http://{ip}:8080

'
  fixtureModeGeneral: 'DMX Mode selects how this fixture interprets DMX data.



    Each
    mode uses a different channel layout and is designed

    for different lighting
    applications.



    Surface Mode:

    For projection mapping onto surfaces.



    Moving
    Head Mode:

    Simulates a beam-style moving head fixture.



    Pixel Mapping
    Mode:

    Allows the fixture to function as a pixel grid

    for LED-style
    pixel mapping.'
  standardMode: "Surface Mode is intended for projecting onto surfaces.\r\n\r\nThe
    Fixture Amount setting can be used to add additional surfaces.  \r\nEach surface
    uses 16 DMX channels. Each added fixture adds another 16 channels.\r\n\r\nChannel
    Mapping:\r\n\r\nCH 1: Master Dimmer\r\nCH 2: Red\r\nCH 3: Green\r\nCH 4: Blue\r\nCH
    5: Pattern Select (16 patterns, 0 = full color)\r\nCH 6: Pattern Parameter\r\nCH
    7: Pattern Animation Speed\r\nCH 8: Strobe\r\n\r\nCH 9\u201316: Corner Pinning
    X and Y\r\n(Referenced from the bottom-left corner of the screen)"
  movingHeadMode: 'Moving Head Mode is intended for viewing the beam itself

    (using
    haze or smoke).



    This mode uses 14 DMX channels and mimics the behavior
    of

    a standard moving head fixture.



    Channel Mapping:



    CH 1:
    Master Dimmer

    CH 2: Red

    CH 3: Green

    CH 4: Blue

    CH 5: Pan

    CH
    6: Pan Fine

    CH 7: Tilt

    CH 8: Tilt Fine

    CH 9: Pattern / Gobo Select

    CH
    10: Pattern / Gobo Animation Speed

    CH 11: Pattern Scale

    CH 12: Iris
    / Mask Scale

    CH 13: Pattern / Gobo Rotation

    CH 14: Strobe'
  pixelMappingMode: "Pixel Mapping Mode allows the fixture to function as a virtual
    pixel wall.\r\n\r\nThis mode reserves 10 DMX channels for Dimmer, Strobe,\r\nand
    Corner Pinning.\r\n\r\nChannels starting from channel 11 are used as RGB channels\r\nfor
    each pixel.\r\n\r\nThe number of pixels can be configured by adjusting\r\nRows
    and Columns in increments of 8 pixels.\r\n\r\nChannel Mapping:\r\n\r\nCH 1: Master
    Dimmer\r\nCH 2: Strobe\r\nCH 3\u201310: Corner Pinning X and Y\r\n(Referenced
    from the bottom-left corner of the screen)\r\n\r\nCH 11+: RGB channels for each
    pixel"
  universe: 'The DMX universe this fixture listens to.



    This setting determines
    which universe

    the fixture receives DMX data from.



    Universe numbering
    is 1-based.'
  startChannel: 'The first DMX channel this fixture responds to.

    All other channels
    are calculated sequentially from this starting channel.'
  performance: 'Performance depends on the hardware used.



    Higher fixture counts
    or large pixel grids may

    reduce performance on low-power devices.



    For
    best results, use wired Ethernet and

    limit the number of active fixtures
    if needed.'
  fixtureAmount: 'The Fixture Amount setting adds additional virtual fixtures

    for
    surface mapping.



    Each additional surface behaves like a 16-channel fixture.



    *
    Depending on the hardware used in your projector,

    a high number of fixtures
    may reduce performance.'
  pixelRows: The number of rows used for the pixel grid.
  pixelColumns: The number of columns used for the pixel grid.
  networkWarning: 'Toggle the network warning banner on or off.



    The warning
    banner appears when the fixture

    does not receive DMX data for 2 seconds.'
  passwordProtection: 'Password protection restricts access to the Web UI.



    Only
    devices with the correct password can modify

    settings through the Web UI.



    The
    Show button reveals the password for 3 seconds.



    The Set/Reset Password
    button allows the user

    to set or change the password.



    * The password
    is stored internally as plain text

    and is not hashed. Do not use sensitive
    passwords.'
  infoPanel: Toggle the info panel on or off.
  infoPanelDefault: Default message shown in the info panel.
  purchases: 'Open the in app purchases menu to unlock premium features '
  networkModeSAcn: sACN (Streaming Architecture for Control Networks), standardized
    as ANSI E1.31, is a protocol that transmits DMX lighting data over IP networks
    using UDP multicast or unicast
  networkModeArtNet: Art-Net is a communication protocol used to transmit DMX512-A
    lighting control data and Remote Device Management (RDM) signals over an Ethernet
    network using the UDP protocol.
  transportMode: 'sACN (ANSI E1.31) uses UDP as its transport protocol and operates
    in two primary modes:



    Multicast (Default): The most common mode, where
    data is sent to a multicast IP address (e.g., 239.255.0.1) on UDP port 5568. 
    This allows multiple receivers to subscribe to a specific universe efficiently,
    reducing network load through IGMP snooping.



    Unicast: Data is sent directly
    to a specific device''s IP address. This mode also uses UDP, with port 5568 as
    the default, though many implementations allow a configurable port. '
  listenPort: 'The listen port for sACN (ANSI E1.31) depends on the transport mode:



    Multicast
    Mode: Receivers must listen on UDP port 5568.  This port is fixed and cannot
    be changed for multicast transmission.



    Unicast Mode: The listen port is
    configurable.  While port 5568 is often used by default, the receiver can be
    set to listen on any available UDP port as specified by the sender and receiver
    configuration'
  timeoutSeconds: 'The standard timeout for sACN (ANSI E1.31) is 2.5 seconds.  If
    a receiver does not receive any valid sACN packets for a specific universe within
    this period, it considers the source lost. '
  receiveNetworkData: Toggle the receiver on or off
  mergeMode: "HTP (Highest Takes Precedence): When multiple sources transmit to the
    same universe at the same priority, the receiver outputs the highest DMX value
    for each channel.  This is the standard merge algorithm defined by ANSI E1.31
    and is suitable for intensity control. \n\r\nLTP (Latest Takes Precedence): When
    enabled, the receiver outputs the most recently received DMX value for each channel,
    regardless of its numerical value.  This mode is not part of the ANSI E1.31 standard
    and is implemented at the receiver level.  It is typically used for non-intensity
    parameters (e.g., pan, tilt) where the latest command should take effect."
